50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are Textiles, City Under Excavation, Light and Motion, and Maritime Trade. I lean toward Textiles or Excavation for the volunteers.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Shion,,Light and Motion is too risky given the maintenance logs. Maritime Trade sounds like a shipping nightmare.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,May,,City Under Excavation has a working conservation bench! That fits the visitor data perfectly.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Excavation might be too heavy for the bay. Textiles is safer, but the conservation bench in B is a great draw.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Textiles sounds cozy, but the ""working bench"" in City Under Excavation sounds like a fun mystery for visitors!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, if the conservation bench is ""visible"" but not adding to the lab's actual backlog, it could work.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, if the excavation finds are small enough, the weight limit isn't an issue. It's better than the rigging for Light and Motion.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the visitors want to see the process. City Under Excavation provides that without needing a huge staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. As long as the reconstructions aren't too heavy, B is a strong choice.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I vote for the one with the bench! It sounds the most exciting and probably doesn't need expensive shipping.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I think I can support City Under Excavation. It utilizes the history circle's interests well.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It is the most logical choice. Low risk of shipping delays compared to Maritime, and more stable than Light and Motion.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,May,,It's a win for the visitors. I'm fully on board with B.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. It balances the gallery's physical constraints with the public's interest.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! Everyone likes the excavation one!,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
